.Dd 2025-09-30
.Dt PKCS12_DECRYPT_SKEY 3ossl
.Os
.Sh NAME
.Nm PKCS12_decrypt_skey ,
.Nm PKCS12_decrypt_skey_ex
.Nd PKCS12 shrouded keyBag decrypt functions
.Sh SYNOPSIS
.In openssl/pkcs12.h
.Ft PKCS8_PRIV_KEY_INFO *
.Fo PKCS12_decrypt_skey
.Fa "const PKCS12_SAFEBAG *bag"
.Fa "const char *pass"
.Fa "int passlen"
.Fc
.Ft PKCS8_PRIV_KEY_INFO *
.Fo PKCS12_decrypt_skey_ex
.Fa "const PKCS12_SAFEBAG *bag"
.Fa "const char *pass"
.Fa "int passlen"
.Fa "OSSL_LIB_CTX *ctx"
.Fa "const char *propq"
.Fc
.Sh DESCRIPTION
.Fn PKCS12_decrypt_skey
Decrypt the PKCS#8 shrouded keybag contained within
.Fa bag
using the supplied password
.Fa pass
of length
.Fa passlen .
.Pp
.Fn PKCS12_decrypt_skey_ex
is similar to the above but allows for a library context
.Fa ctx
and property query
.Fa propq
to be used to select algorithm implementations.
.Sh RETURN VALUES
Both functions will return the decrypted key or NULL if an error
occurred.
.Sh CONFORMING TO
IETF RFC 7292
.Pf ( Lk https://tools.ietf.org/html/rfc7292 )
.Sh SEE ALSO
.Xr PKCS8_decrypt_ex 3 ,
.Xr PKCS8_encrypt_ex 3 ,
.Xr PKCS12_add_key_ex 3 ,
.Xr PKCS12_SAFEBAG_create_pkcs8_encrypt_ex 3
.Sh HISTORY
.Fn PKCS12_decrypt_skey_ex
was added in OpenSSL 3.0.
